<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Scenario 05 - SAFE: large time gap (200 m behind merge), both at 60 km/h
At 60 km/h (16.67 m/s) the main car takes 12 s to reach the merge.  The
merging car also at 60 km/h on a 63.4 m ramp reaches the merge in ~3.8 s.
The highway car is nowhere near the merge when the ramp car merges.
Expected: lane_merge_safe (no car in entry zone at trigger time).

OSM edges:
  merging ramp : 353879480 (lane 0, accel) -> 954971261 -> 106116297-AddedOnRampEdge -> 106116297
  highway main : 497720156 (lane 1, through) -> 353879480 -> ...-> 106116297

In the synthetic network highway_in was only 182.5 m, so a 7 s depart delay was
used to simulate 200 m.  On the OSM network 497720156 is 211.36 m, so the 200 m
gap is representable directly: 305.72 - 200 = 105.72 m into 497720156.
-->
<routes>
    <vType id="car" accel="2.6" decel="4.5" sigma="0.0" length="4.5"
           maxSpeed="33.33" minGap="2.5"/>

    <vehicle id="merging_car" type="car" depart="0.0"
             departLane="0" departPos="30.96" departSpeed="16.67">
        <route edges="353879480 954971261 106116297-AddedOnRampEdge 106116297"/>
    </vehicle>

    <!-- 200 m before merge on through-lane; 305.72 - 200 = 105.72 -->
    <vehicle id="main_car" type="car" depart="0.0"
             departLane="1" departPos="105.72" departSpeed="16.67">
        <route edges="497720156 353879480 954971261 106116297-AddedOnRampEdge 106116297"/>
    </vehicle>
</routes>
